# Citation metadata. GitHub renders a "Cite this repository" button from this
# file, and it is what makes the repo citable from a paper or a talk.
cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Churn vs Risk: a runnable POC"
message: "If you use this software or its findings, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Shinde
    given-names: Santosh
repository-code: "https://github.com/santoshshinde2012/churn-vs-risk-poc"
abstract: >-
  Runnable companion code for the article "Why Your Churn Model Is Not a Risk
  Model (And Why It Matters)". Builds a batch churn pipeline and a real-time
  fraud pipeline end to end and empirically tests twenty claims about how the
  two differ, including label maturation, point-in-time correctness, cost-based
  thresholds, selective labels, uplift targeting and label-free drift detection.
  Three of the article's claims are qualified or contradicted by the results and
  are reported as such.
keywords:
  - machine-learning
  - churn-prediction
  - fraud-detection
  - mlops
  - selective-labels
  - uplift-modeling
  - model-calibration
  - drift-detection
  - databricks
license: Apache-2.0
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-08-13"
